    "## 1. My lane (or freestyle) and why\n",
    "\n",
    "**Lane chosen: Lane 2 — Refresh / Content Opportunity Scoring**\n",
    "\n",
    "The question this lane answers is: *which pages should be reviewed first for refresh, based on observable search and engagement signals?*\n",
    "\n",
    "I chose this lane because it maps directly to a real capacity problem: content teams cannot manually review tens of thousands of pages, so the decision of *what to look at first* is itself high-stakes. The starter dataset already contains the signals this lane needs — impressions, sessions, position, CTR, age, trend direction — and the verified starter results show that a learned ranking beats a fixed rule by a wide margin on Precision@50. That gap is the motivating number: it means the ranking a human reviewer actually follows can be made 3× more accurate with a model, without changing the review process itself. I am building at FlyRankAI, which is a product that helps teams prioritize content work, so this lane is also the one closest to what I ship."
